<article class="env-lemma" id="0DWC">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0DWC">Lemma <span data-tag="0DWC">47.22.2</span>.</a> Let $A \to B$ be a flat map of Noetherian rings. Let $I \subset A$ be an ideal such that $A/I = B/IB$ and such that $IB$ is contained in the Jacobson radical of $B$. Let $\omega _ A^\bullet $ be a dualizing complex. Then $\omega _ A^\bullet \otimes _ A B$ is a dualizing complex for $B$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      It is clear that $\omega _ A^\bullet \otimes _ A B$ is in $D^ b_{\textit{Coh}}(B)$. By More on Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/0A6A" data-tag="0A6A">15.101.2</a> we see that 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  R\mathop{\mathrm{Hom}}\nolimits _ B(K \otimes _ A B, \omega _ A^\bullet \otimes _ A B) = R\mathop{\mathrm{Hom}}\nolimits _ A(K, \omega _ A^\bullet ) \otimes _ A B  \]
</div>
    <p>
       for any $K \in D^ b_{\textit{Coh}}(A)$. For any ideal $IB \subset J \subset B$ there is a unique ideal $I \subset J' \subset A$ such that $A/J' \otimes _ A B = B/J$. Thus $\omega _ A^\bullet \otimes _ A B$ has finite injective dimension by More on Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/0DW2" data-tag="0DW2">15.71.6</a>. Finally, we also have 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  R\mathop{\mathrm{Hom}}\nolimits _ B(\omega _ A^\bullet \otimes _ A B, \omega _ A^\bullet \otimes _ A B) = R\mathop{\mathrm{Hom}}\nolimits _ A(\omega _ A^\bullet , \omega _ A^\bullet ) \otimes _ A B = A \otimes _ A B = B  \]
</div>
    <p>
       as desired. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>